  "claim_boundary": {
    "proves": [
      "Two distinct canonical, physically valid positions generated through legal moves have the same current 30-bit production primary hash.",
      "With the exact production WASM and current live weights, deliberately retaining A's cache state before searching B causes the primary-only TT lookup to reuse A's root key and score.",
      "The reused key is not legal in B, while clearing the caches before B returns a legal and different result."
    ],
    "does_not_prove": [
      "The frequency of harmful primary-hash collisions in ordinary live games.",
      "That an illegal root key has been observed in production traffic or in the completed bounded quiet-history match.",
      "A separate evaluation-cache collision effect isolated from the TT effect.",
      "That a particular secondary-lock implementation is correct, fast enough, or stronger.",
      "Any Elo, dan-rank, direct-play, external-calibration, or production-promotion result."
    ],
